==============================================================================
3. AREA SPLITTING: 'A BIG BLOB IS PROBABLY TWO CELLS'
==============================================================================
  threshold 0.40: best so far valid   26.9 at cell area  90 px
  threshold 0.50: best so far valid   21.5 at cell area  90 px
  threshold 0.60: best so far valid   11.1 at cell area  60 px
  threshold 0.70: best so far valid   11.1 at cell area  60 px
best: threshold 0.60, divisor 60 px -> valid 11.1, test 12.7, bias -5.5 cells. This is the hypothesis the task is built on, working as an explicit rule: a bright region of twice the area is counted as two cells. Counting the same blobs as they are gives 85.4 on test, so the split alone is worth 72.8 cells. The divisor it wants (60 px) is smaller than a lone cell (126 px), because at this threshold every cell sits inside a fattened sheet - section 5's saturation, absorbed into one fitted number.

